// Title: Shell Process Spawned by Java.EXE
// Sigma ID: dff1e1cc-d3fd-47c8-bfc2-aeb878a754c0
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades), Nasreddine Bencherchali
// Date: 2021-12-17 | Modified: 2024-01-18
// ATT&CK: initial-access, persistence, privilege-escalation
// Description: Detects shell spawned from Java host process, which could be a sign of exploitation (e.g. log4j
//   exploitation)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate calls to system binaries
//   - Company specific internal usage
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20231230220738/https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_java_susp_child_process_2.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\java.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\bash.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe")) and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "build" and ProcessCommandLine contains "build")))
